WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.709 --> 00:00:18.400
The brown bear, Baloo, began teaching Mowgli the law of the jungle.

2
00:00:20.001 --> 00:00:22.463
He showed the boy where to find good nuts.

3
00:00:24.704 --> 00:00:29.408
He taught him not to bother Mang, the bat, while he slept during the day.

4
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:36.281
Mowgli also learned to warn the water snakes before he splashed into their pool.

5
00:00:39.922 --> 00:00:43.623
Each day Bagheera came to check on Mowgli's progress.

6
00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:46.684
"Mowgli is amazing!"

7
00:00:47.144 --> 00:00:48.605
Baloo said, beaming.

8
00:00:49.445 --> 00:00:51.686
"He climbs as well as he swims.

9
00:00:52.246 --> 00:00:55.027
And he swims almost as well as he runs."

10
00:00:57.447 --> 00:00:59.968
Baloo made Mowgli work very hard.

11
00:01:04.552 --> 00:01:06.553
One day Mowgli got bored.

12
00:01:09.194 --> 00:01:13.276
When Baloo scolded him for being lazy, Mowgli ran off.

13
00:01:18.958 --> 00:01:19.899
"Where's the boy?"

14
00:01:20.359 --> 00:01:22.300
Bagheera asked when he arrived.

15
00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:24.161
Baloo sighed.

16
00:01:24.181 --> 00:01:27.042
"He went off in a huff."

17
00:01:28.182 --> 00:01:31.464
"The man cub is very young," Bagheera said.

18
00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:36.153
"Maybe his head is too little to remember all these things."

19
00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:40.194
"Well, he's not too little to be killed!"

20
00:01:40.614 --> 00:01:41.554
Baloo replied.

21
00:01:41.574 --> 00:01:45.015
"That's why I'm teaching him the law of the jungle.

22
00:01:46.096 --> 00:01:49.116
He's even learning all of the languages of the jungle.

23
00:01:49.937 --> 00:01:52.537
This will protect him and keep him safe here."

24
00:01:52.557 --> 00:01:59.059
"Maybe." Bagheera stretched out a paw to admire his sharp claws.

25
00:02:00.460 --> 00:02:06.558
"When we find Mowgli, I'll ask him to show you his skill with the languages," Baloo said.

26
00:02:06.578 --> 00:02:09.660
"But who knows when he'll return."

27
00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:12.001
"I'm right here!"

28
00:02:12.562 --> 00:02:14.143
a voice snapped from above.

29
00:02:15.883 --> 00:02:19.205
Mowgli slid down a tree trunk and glared at Baloo.

30
00:02:19.225 --> 00:02:22.987
"I only came down because of Bagheera.

31
00:02:23.508 --> 00:02:26.149
I'm still mad at you, fat old Baloo!"

32
00:02:26.169 --> 00:02:32.428
"Show Bagheera how you can speak the jungle languages," Baloo said.

33
00:02:32.448 --> 00:02:34.369
"Which one?

34
00:02:35.089 --> 00:02:38.091
I know all of them," Mowgli boasted.

35
00:02:38.111 --> 00:02:42.212
"Okay, great scholar," Baloo teased him.

36
00:02:42.232 --> 00:02:45.774
"Why don't you speak like the lion?"

37
00:02:47.474 --> 00:02:49.395
Mowgli spoke in a deep voice.

38
00:02:50.496 --> 00:02:52.756
"We are of one blood."

39
00:02:52.776 --> 00:02:55.458
"Good," Baloo said.

40
00:02:55.478 --> 00:02:58.339
"Now speak like a bird."

41
00:02:59.559 --> 00:03:01.260
Mowgli made a hawk's call.

42
00:03:03.504 --> 00:03:04.805
Bagheera was impressed.

43
00:03:04.825 --> 00:03:09.367
"Now the snake's language."

44
00:03:13.308 --> 00:03:14.048
Mowgli said.

45
00:03:15.429 --> 00:03:19.891
He clapped for his own performance and then jumped onto Bagheera's back.

46
00:03:20.871 --> 00:03:25.993
He banged his heels on the panther's sides while making nasty faces at Baloo.

47
00:03:26.013 --> 00:03:30.375
"Someday you will thank me," Baloo muttered.

48
00:03:30.395 --> 00:03:34.622
"Baloo, how did you learn all the languages?"

49
00:03:35.122 --> 00:03:36.163
Bagheera asked.

50
00:03:37.264 --> 00:03:40.547
The bear patted his big furry stomach proudly.

51
00:03:40.567 --> 00:03:43.669
"I learned them from Hathi the elephant."

52
00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:49.194
Meanwhile Mowgli was kicking Bagheera and grabbing at his fur.

53
00:03:49.214 --> 00:03:51.996
"Hey!" Bagheera said.

54
00:03:52.016 --> 00:03:54.358
"Watch out for my ribs."

55
00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.264
"Someday I'll have a whole tribe of my own," Mowgli bragged.

56
00:04:01.868 --> 00:04:03.989
"I'll lead everyone through the jungle.

57
00:04:04.569 --> 00:04:07.069
I'll play and eat all day long."

58
00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:08.510
He laughed.

59
00:04:08.530 --> 00:04:13.351
"And I'll throw branches and dirt at old Baloo."

60
00:04:17.092 --> 00:04:22.034
Whoof! Baloo's big paw scooped Mowgli off Bagheera's back.

61
00:04:26.635 --> 00:04:27.355
Baloo said.

62
00:04:27.375 --> 00:04:29.996
"You sound just like the monkeys.

63
00:04:30.348 --> 00:04:32.149
You've been spending time with them!"

64
00:04:32.949 --> 00:04:34.390
Mowgli lay on the ground.

65
00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:38.491
He looked at Bagheera, whose eyes had turned cold.

66
00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:41.593
"The monkeys have no laws.

67
00:04:42.053 --> 00:04:44.674
They are rude and silly," Baloo said.

68
00:04:44.694 --> 00:04:48.656
"Stay away from them!"

69
00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:51.037
Mowgli sniffled.

70
00:04:51.857 --> 00:04:53.618
"You were mean to me before.

71
00:04:54.178 --> 00:04:55.679
But the monkeys were nice.

72
00:04:56.399 --> 00:04:58.840
They came down from the trees and played with me.

73
00:04:59.320 --> 00:05:00.901
They gave me nuts too."

74
00:05:02.242 --> 00:05:03.202
Baloo snorted.

75
00:05:03.222 --> 00:05:10.966
"They said I'm going to be their leader one day," Mowgli added spitefully.

76
00:05:10.986 --> 00:05:15.048
"They have no leader," Bagheera snapped.

77
00:05:15.068 --> 00:05:16.689
"And they lie."

78
00:05:19.711 --> 00:05:20.611
"Listen, Mowgli."

79
00:05:21.152 --> 00:05:23.513
Baloo's voice rumbled like thunder.

80
00:05:23.533 --> 00:05:26.374
"The monkeys live in the trees.

81
00:05:26.875 --> 00:05:29.016
They boast and chatter constantly.

82
00:05:30.004 --> 00:05:32.445
We do not drink where the monkeys drink.

83
00:05:32.885 --> 00:05:35.526
We do not go where the monkeys go."

84
00:05:36.566 --> 00:05:38.147
Mowgli lay very still.

85
00:05:39.087 --> 00:05:42.528
"We do not notice them," Baloo added.

86
00:05:42.548 --> 00:05:45.769
"Even when they throw nuts on our heads!"

87
00:05:46.849 --> 00:05:50.030
Just then nuts poured down from the trees.

88
00:05:51.151 --> 00:05:54.312
A bunch of monkeys howled loudly with laughter.
